# Lead timeline parity (web ↔ mobile)

The lead **Timeline** on web (`CRM-project`) and mobile (`crm_mobile`) must stay behaviorally aligned. When you change timeline grouping, entry types, chips, or WhatsApp presentation on one client, update the other in the same change set (or immediately after).

## Canonical sources

| Concern | Web | Mobile |
|---------|-----|--------|
| Build + merge events | `CRM-project/pages/ViewLeadPage.tsx` | `lib/utils/timeline_builder.dart` (`buildLeadTimeline`) |
| Entry model / types | `CRM-project/types.ts` | `lib/models/timeline_entry.dart` |
| Render | `CRM-project/components/Timeline.tsx` | `lib/widgets/lead_timeline.dart` |
| Copy EN/AR | `CRM-project/constants.ts` | `lib/core/localization/app_localizations.dart` |

## WhatsApp quieter timeline (required parity)

- Map each WA message with `direction` (`inbound` / `outbound`).
- After merging all sources, sort chronologically and **collapse consecutive** `whatsapp` rows into one `whatsappThread` card (`collapseConsecutiveWhatsAppThreads` in `timeline_builder.dart`).
- Non-WhatsApp events (call, visit, SMS, stage, etc.) **break** the group.
- Thread card: green WhatsApp chip, conversation title + count, latest-message preview, expand/collapse compact `←`/`→` lines, phone once with LTR (`forceLtr` on stage chip).
- Default **collapsed**.
- Web has **Open in Chats**; mobile uses `onOpenWhatsAppChat` on `LeadTimeline` → `WhatsAppChatThreadScreen` when the user has WhatsApp chat access.

## Social quieter timeline (required parity)

Instagram DM / Messenger, from `getLeadSocialMessages` (`GET /integrations/inbox/lead-messages/?client=`).

- Map each social message with `direction`, plus `socialChannel` and `socialConversationId` from the row.
- Collapse consecutive `social` rows into one `socialThread` card (`collapseConsecutiveSocialThreads` in `timeline_builder.dart`), run **after** the WhatsApp collapse on the same merged list.
- **A change of conversation breaks the group**, unlike WhatsApp which groups on adjacency alone. A lead can hold an Instagram DM and a Messenger thread at once; merging them would file two strangers under one heading.
- Thread card: pink chip labelled with the **network** (Instagram / Messenger, not "Inbox"), conversation title + count, latest-message preview, expand/collapse compact `←`/`→` lines. Default **collapsed**.
- `stage` holds the contact handle, not a phone — do **not** set `forceLtr` on its stage chip.
- Media-only messages have an empty body; `localizeSocialMessageBody` substitutes a placeholder (parity with web `socialMessageBodyDisplay.ts`).
- Both platforms link to the Inbox **list**, not a preselected thread: mobile `onOpenSocialInbox` → `SocialInboxListScreen` gated on `canAccessSocialInbox`, web `goToPage('Inbox')`.
- `getLeadSocialMessages` returns `[]` on 403/404 rather than throwing — reception/data entry are denied by the inbox ACL and that must not blank the whole timeline.

## Rules of thumb

- Same event sources and sort key (`timestamp`); prefer shared sort preference key `leadTimelineSortOrder`.
- Do not leave mobile on one full card per WA message while web uses thread cards (or the reverse).
- Prefer frontend-only grouping unless both clients need new API fields.
